subproblems.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, let τ : Fin n → ℝ^P be orthonormal, and let w ∈ NVector (Eucl P) n satisfy w = simpleNVector τ or w = −simpleNVector τ. Here simpleNVector τ = τ_1 ∧ ⋯ ∧ τ_n is the functional b ↦ b(τ_1, …, τ_n). Then:
(i) |w(b)| ≤ ‖b‖ for every n-covector b ∈ Covector (Eucl P) n, where ‖b‖ is the operator norm of the continuous alternating map b;
(ii) w ≠ 0.

Let P ∈ ℕ and let μ be a measure on ℝ^P (Borel σ-algebra). Let M, W ⊆ ℝ^P with W open and M μ-null-measurable, let θ, g : ℝ^P → ℝ, and let C ∈ ℝ. Assume:
(i) θ(x) > 0 for every x ∈ M;
(ii) θ is μ-integrable on M ∩ W;
(iii) g is a.e.-strongly measurable for μ⌞M = μ.restrict M;
(iv) |g(x)| ≤ C for μ⌞M-a.e. x;
(v) ∫_M θ(x)·(φ(x)·g(x)) dμ(x) = 0 for every C^∞ function φ : ℝ^P → ℝ with compact support and tsupport φ ⊆ W.
Then for μ⌞M-a.e. x, x ∈ W implies g(x) = 0.

Let P, n ∈ ℕ and U, W ⊆ ℝ^P, and let T ∈ D_n(U) (T : GeometricCurrentOn U n). Let M ⊆ ℝ^P, θ : ℝ^P → ℝ and ξ : ℝ^P → NVector (Eucl P) n satisfy IsRectifiableTriple U n M θ ξ:
- M ⊆ U is Hⁿ-null-measurable and countably n-rectifiable;
- θ > 0 on M, and θ is Hⁿ-integrable on M ∩ K for every compact K ⊆ U;
- ξ is Hⁿ⌞M-a.e. strongly measurable;
- for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ M there is an orthonormal τ : Fin n → ℝ^P such that span τ is a weighted approximate tangent space of (M, θ) at x and ξ(x) = ±simpleNVector τ.
Assume T(ω) = τ(M, θ, ξ)(ω) = ∫_M θ(x)·ξ(x)(ω(x)) dHⁿ(x) for every ω ∈ Dⁿ(U). Assume also that W is open, closure W is compact, closure W ⊆ U, and T vanishes on W (T(ψ) = 0 for every ψ ∈ Dⁿ(U) with tsupport ψ ⊆ W). Then Hⁿ(M ∩ W) = 0, where Hⁿ = μHE[n].
